# IWXXM Domain Vocabulary

Use terms from `docs/feature-list.md` and `docs/spec.md` consistently.

## Correct Terms

| Term | Meaning | Use instead of |
|------|---------|----------------|
| METAR | Routine aviation weather report (TAC) | "weather text", "report string" |
| SPECI | Special METAR (TAC) | "special report" |
| TAC | Traditional Alphanumeric Code (raw METAR/SPECI text) | "raw text", "plain text" |
| IWXXM | WMO XML aviation weather exchange format | "XML output", "weather XML" |
| GIFTs | Library converting TAC → IWXXM | "converter lib", "parser" |
| vendor/schemas | Authoritative read-only wmo-im schema snapshots | "schemas submodule", "local XSD edits" |
| IWXXM version | Release line (e.g. 2023-1, 2025-2) | "schema version" (ambiguous) |
| Conversion | TAC → IWXXM transformation (F1) | "parsing" alone (validation is separate) |
| Validation | XSD + Schematron check on IWXXM (F2) | "lint", "check XML" |

## Component Names

- `packages/gifts` — not `GIFTs/` submodule path in new docs/code comments
- `apps/backend` — hosts `/api/v1/convert`, `/api/v1/validate`, and `/auth/*`
- `vendor/manifest.json` — pins wmo-im repo + tag/SHA per schema bundle

## Version Handling (F4)

- Target version is a user-selected IWXXM release line present in `vendor/schemas/`
- Version-aware formatting follows `docs/IWXXM_VERSION_SWITCHING.md`

When introducing new domain terms, back-add to `docs/feature-list.md` or raise `[Ambiguity]`.
